islation to reflect the introduction of the Carer \nSupport Payment (CSP) which replaces CA in Scotland.\nNote:\n This guidance is applicable to UC, JSA and ESA.","tree_line_end":552,"tree_line_start":537},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nCA (CSP)(Scot) Regs 23 (CA) Order 23","tree_line_end":564,"tree_line_start":553},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Social Fund Funeral Payment ","tree_line_end":571,"tree_line_start":565},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3.\n \n \nADM L3408\n and \nAppendix 1 to ADM Chapter L3\n gives guidance on arrears of benefit payable to the \ndeceased not being counted as assets of the deceased when considering deductions from the \namount of award of funeral payment. From 19.11.23 arrears of CSP payable to the deceased as at the \ndate of death are excluded from the assets of the deceased\n1\n.","tree_line_end":596,"tree_line_start":572},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1\n   \nSFMFE (Gen) Regs, reg 10(1A)(ca)  ","tree_line_end":608,"tree_line_start":597},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Universal Credit","tree_line_end":615,"tree_line_start":609},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":" \n \n \n \nThe carer element","tree_line_end":625,"tree_line_start":616},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":629,"tree_line_start":626},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"4. \nADM F6033\n gives guidance that when considering whether a carer element is payable, w\nhere two or \nmore people are regularly and substantially caring for the same severely disabled person, only one of \nthem will be entitled to have the carer element included in the UC award. From 19.11.23 regulations\n1\n \nprovide\n \nthat w\nhere a \n \n ","tree_line_end":651,"tree_line_start":630},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n1.\n \n \nperson (A) has an entitlement to CSP \nand\n ","tree_line_end":671,"tree_line_start":652},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n2.\n \n \nperson (B) has an entitlement to the carer element of UC\n \nthey must jointly elect who shall have entitlement to the carer element. If there is no such election, the \nSecretary of State, in consultation with the Scottish Ministers, shall decide.","tree_line_end":691,"tree_line_start":672},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":695,"tree_line_start":692},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nUC regs, reg 29(5)(6)\n; \nCA (CSP)(Scot) Regs 23 (CA) Order 23","tree_line_end":713,"tree_line_start":696},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":720,"tree_line_start":714},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":724,"tree_line_start":721},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":" \n \n \nRegular and substantial caring responsibilities","tree_line_end":733,"tree_line_start":725},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":737,"tree_line_start":734},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"5. \nADM F6010\n gives guidance that to qualify for an award of a carer element, the claimant must have \nregular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person and would meet that \ncondition if they satisfy the conditions for entitlement to a CA\n1\n. From 19.11.23 regulations\n2\n adds to the \nlist\n ","tree_line_end":758,"tree_line_start":738},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n1.\n those who would be entitled to a CA but for the fact that\n ","tree_line_end":771,"tree_line_start":759},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n1.1\n \n \n \ntheir earnings exceed the prescribed limits \nor\n ","tree_line_end":795,"tree_line_start":772},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n1.2\n \n \n \nthey are resident or treated as resident in Scotland \nor\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n1.3\n \n \n \nthey have a genuine and sufficient link to Scotland \nand\n ","tree_line_end":840,"tree_line_start":796},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n 2.\n \n those entitled to CSP.","tree_line_end":853,"tree_line_start":841},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":857,"tree_line_start":854},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nUC Regs, reg 30(1)\n; 2\n \nCA (CSP)(Scot) Regs 23 (CA) Order 23","tree_line_end":877,"tree_line_start":858},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":884,"tree_line_start":878},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":" \n \n \nEntitlement to a housing cost element – renters exempt from HCC\n \n \n ","tree_line_end":899,"tree_line_start":885},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"6. \nADM F3151\n gives guidance on considering whether a renter is exempt from a HCC deduction. From \n19.11.23 CSP is added to the list of relevant benefits the renter may be in receipt of to be exempt\n1\n.","tree_line_end":913,"tree_line_start":900},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":917,"tree_line_start":914},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nUC Regs, Sch 4, para 16(2  \n)  \n ","tree_line_end":934,"tree_line_start":918},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":" \n \n \n \n Unearned income ","tree_line_end":945,"tree_line_start":935},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"7. \n \n \nCSP is taken into account as unearned income up to a maximum of the amount a claimant would \nreceive if they had an entitlement to CA\n1\n.","tree_line_end":959,"tree_line_start":946},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nUC Regs, reg 66(1)(b)(iiia)","tree_line_end":971,"tree_line_start":960},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":975,"tree_line_start":972},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Jobseeker’s allowance","tree_line_end":982,"tree_line_start":976},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":" \n \n \nWaiting days","tree_line_end":993,"tree_line_start":983},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"8.\n \n \n \nADM R2702\n gives guidance on when a JSA claimant does not have to serve waiting days. From \n19.11.23 CSP is added to the list of qualifying benefits\n1\n.","tree_line_end":1012,"tree_line_start":994},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nJSA Regs 13, reg 36(1)","tree_line_end":1024,"tree_line_start":1013},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":" \n \n \n \nLinked periods","tree_line_end":1035,"tree_line_start":1025},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n9. \nADM R1027\n gives guidance on linked periods. From 19.11.23 a linked period will include when a \nclaimant is entitled to a CSP\n1\n. \n \n ","tree_line_end":1054,"tree_line_start":1036},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nJSA Regs 13, reg 39(2)\n; \nSS CB Act 92, s 70 ","tree_line_end":1072,"tree_line_start":1055},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1079,"tree_line_start":1073},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":" \n \n \nCarers and remunerative work","tree_line_end":1090,"tree_line_start":1080},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"10. \n \nFor the purpose of whether a JSA claimant is in remunerative work where they are a carer\n1\n \n(see \nR2252\n), CSP\n2\n is added to the list of qualifying benefits from 19.11.23. See\n \nChapter R2  \n   \n(JSA conditions of \nentitlement) for further details.","tree_line_end":1118,"tree_line_start":1091},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nJSA Regs 13, reg 42(3)(c)(iii)\n; 2 \nCA (CSP)(Scot) Regs 23 (CA) Order 23","tree_line_end":1136,"tree_line_start":1119},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1143,"tree_line_start":1137},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Employment and Support Allowance","tree_line_end":1149,"tree_line_start":1144},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n ","tree_line_end":1163,"tree_line_start":1150},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":" \n \n \nFirst contribution condition","tree_line_end":1174,"tree_line_start":1164},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"11. \n \nU1085\n gives guidance on relaxation of the first contribution condition\n1\n where specified conditions \nare met, including where the ESA claimant is entitled to CA in the last complete tax year immediately \nbefore the relevant benefit year in which the first day of LCW occurred\n2\n. From 19.11.23 this includes \nwhere the claimant is entitled to CSP\n3\n.","tree_line_end":1199,"tree_line_start":1175},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nWR Act 07, Sch 1, Part 1, para 1(4)(b)\n;\n \n \n2 \nESA Regs 13, reg 9(2)(a)\n; ","tree_line_end":1221,"tree_line_start":1200},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3 \nCA (CSP)(Scot) Regs 23 (CA) Order 23","tree_line_end":1231,"tree_line_start":1222},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1238,"tree_line_start":1232},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":" \n \n \n \n \nWaiting days","tree_line_end":1251,"tree_line_start":1239},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"12.\n \n \nU1303\n gives guidance on when an ESA claimant does not have to serve waiting days, including where \nentitlement to ESA begins within 12 weeks of the end of entitlement to specified benefits\n1\n. From \n19.11.23, CSP\n2\n is added to the list of qualifying benefits.","tree_line_end":1272,"tree_line_start":1252},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nESA Regs 13, reg 85(2)(a)\n; 2 \nCA (CSP)(Scot) Regs 23 (CA) Order 23","tree_line_end":1290,"tree_line_start":1273},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1297,"tree_line_start":1291},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1303,"tree_line_start":1298},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Universal Credit (Transitional Protections)","tree_line_end":1310,"tree_line_start":1304},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":" \n \n \n Amount of transitional SDP element: joint claimants","tree_line_end":1320,"tree_line_start":1311},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"13. \nMemo ADM 13/23\n paragraphs 6 – 10 gives guidance on the amount of the transitional SDP element \npayable to joint claimants in the first AP where a person has become a carer for either of them in that \nAP\n1\n. From 19.11.23 the definition of carer includes a person who is entitled to and in receipt of CSP\n2\n.","tree_line_end":1339,"tree_line_start":1321},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note:\n See M6710 et seq for detailed guidance on the transitional SDP element.","tree_line_end":1345,"tree_line_start":1340},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nUC (TP) Regs, Sch 2 para 8(2)\n; 2 \nCA (CSP)(Scot) Regs 23 (CA) Order 23","tree_line_end":1363,"tree_line_start"